/-
Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/K4/Law/W/BookAtHead.lean: CONDITIONAL. Five statements with their
proofs, and one private lemma (`five_at`).

What is here. WHAT THE MAKER's BOOK HAS FOR THE MEMBER OF THE FEED-FORWARD LAYERS' OWN ROUNDS
(sub-protocol K4), UNDER THE LIBRARY's HYPOTHESIS h (`AtMgA`, Johnson/P5J/MgAtAll.lean), IN ONE
PLACE: THREE LAWS, each at a group g below 12, at the public data Qp that `k4PubG Zp g` returns
(Lot/PubG.lean), and at a book B that `bookWhole` (Honest/BookWhole.lean, of other writers) returns
at the seated description `F0T` and the list of merges `mergesByName cF.blocksInOrder` (hB). THE LOCK:
`k4Names_at_head_of` (Law/W/LockAtHead.lean): it stands there and is not typed again; its hB stands
at the public part's own three lists of sendings, of which it reads the first; it asks he besides.
LENDS: `k4Lends_at_head_of`: `lendsRow B 0 (k4Place Qp) (k4RowIn Qp) = true`
(Honest/Small/LendsRow.lean): A Bool ON PUBLIC DATA, AT CHAIN NUMBER 0, AT K4's ROW AS IT STANDS
BEFORE IT IS SEATED (`k4RowIn`, Honest/K4/Part.lean): NOT THE RETURN OF `lendRow`
(Honest/Frame.lean, of other writers). THE CUT: `k4Cut_at_head_of`: the book's cut at K4's place is
the list of the numbers of moves of K4's seated row `k4Row`. IN THESE TWO THE THREE LISTS OF
SENDINGS ARE FREE LETTERS p0 p1 p2: their proofs read none of them; the lock's hB is an instance of
theirs. THE FACTS ARE TWO, NOT THREE: LENDS IS ALSO A FIELD OF BOTH NAMES OF THE LOCK
(`K4LastEntry.lends`, Law/W/LastEntry.lean; `K4MaskLock.last`, Law/W/MaskLock.lean). What the law of
its own buys: lends with no he, and with none of the closed evaluations beneath it. Besides:
`k4Member_at_head`: a member of the head's own first chain with K4's place of group g and K4's
table's entries: no book stands in it; that it is the only one is not drawn. Beneath the two, at an
opened description O (`IM.Open`, Johnson/IMR/SeatOpen.lean): `k4Lends_at_record`, `k4Cut_at_record`;
the second at every list of merges M.

How. At O, for lends: the steps of `k4Names_at_record` (Law/W/LockAtMember.lean, of another writer):
`k4_member_there` hands a member b and `k4Counts_at_group` the counts (the same file);
`k4Ends_of_public` (Law/W/MergesByName.lean) two more; the places are distinct by `places_nodup`
(Honest/Law/Cuts.lean, of other writers); `k4_rowIsPlan_byName` and `k4_noSeed`
(Law/W/MergesByName.lean) the form and the fact on the rounds' names; then `k4_lends_whole`
(Law/W/LendsOfBook.lean, of another writer). For the cut: `k4_member_there` and the opening's
equation on the description alone; then `k4_cut_fits` (Law/W/CutAtK4.lean, of another writer). At
the head: its fields scope, reads, laid.opened and laid.planOk, `k4PubG_fields` (Law/W/PubGOf.lean)
with `IM.Open.W`, and `placesOk_of_planOk` (Johnson/RunOne/Sound/KeyListsAtFK.lean).

Not shown here. hB: THAT THE MAKER RETURNS A BOOK THERE: a hypothesis here; under the head
`bookWhole` returns at F0T (`bookWhole_returns_at_head_ahead`,
AtFullSide/K14/WholeAheadAtHead.lean). THAT THE FRAME's MAKER `onlineProverFromPublicFiles`
(Honest/AtPure.lean, of other writers) RETURNS IS NOT SHOWN HERE; nor that B is the book of a
thread. THAT B IS THE BOOK OF WHAT `onlineProverFromPublicFiles` RETURNS: where `onlineProverFromPublicFiles` returns A, `atPure_book_at_head`
(Honest/K14/AtPureBookAtHead.lean, of other writers; read whole by this file's writer) has hB, at
the public part's own three lists, at B := A.B under h: so the three laws hold at A.B there; that
law is called in Law/W/BookAtPure.lean, which has lends, the cut and the lock at A.B itself; not
here. THAT `onlineProverFromPublicFiles` RETURNS IS SHOWN IN NONE OF THESE FILES; OF A THREAD AT A's PROVER NOTHING IS
SAID. `onlineProverFromPublicFiles` calls `bookWhole` at the last three of the seven lists of `sendsOf`: LENDS AND THE
CUT TYPE THERE, AT THE HEAD AND AT O; THE LOCK AT THE HEAD DOES NOT AS IT STANDS; ITS FORM AT O
(`k4Names_at_record_gk`, Law/W/MergeEndsAt.lean) DOES. THAT `mergesByName` IS THE FORMAT's LIST OF
MERGES IS NOT SPOKEN OF. WHAT THE TWO PAY: `chainSteps` (Honest/Frame.lean) refuses at a
sub-protocol with a prover's side for six causes: its lists of rounds and of oracle messages differ
in length; the side has another number of rounds than the block; the cut; a row of the book beyond
the side's parts; an entry of the book beyond them; `lendRow` refuses. THE CUT's LAW SPEAKS TO THE
THIRD, where the side's parts are `k4Row`. THE LAW ON LENDS IS TWO LAWS AWAY FROM THE SIXTH:
`k4_lends_row` (Law/W/LendsK4.lean) carries the Bool to the seated row, `lendsRow_iff`
(Honest/Small/LendsRow.lean) to `lendRow`'s return: this file calls neither. THE OTHER FOUR CAUSES
ARE NOT SPOKEN OF HERE; nor that the prover's side found at K4's place has K4's row. WHAT IS LEFT OF
THE LOCK: that the maker's owners and starts are the senders'. WHAT THE LEMMAS THAT TAKE THE TWO
NAMES ASK BESIDES (`k4MaskOwn_at`, Law/W/MaskLockAt.lean; `k4IndexOwn_at`, Law/W/IndexLockAt.lean),
EACH OF THE SENDER's LOT: hn: the message's number; hA: the sender's text answers at the places that
K4 reads; hE: what it answers is the coin at the owner's address (on the mask row's side from the
start on; on the index's side the one coin at the start); OS: the sender's own lot is `OwnMsgs`;
and, on the mask row's side alone, hL: these places lie below the bound of hE. NONE OF THE NINE IS
SHOWN HERE. The two forms that end in the key turned (`k4MaskTie_at`, `k4IndexTie_at`, the same
files) ask besides Lh and hQ, which h has, and hV and hN on each side and hT on the mask row's: that
the thread stands in front of K4's member, that the sender's Vq holds of its input and that N
challenges are heard: not shown here. On the index's side the like of hT stands in front of that
lemma's end, with three more: the thread stands there, the member's step is taken, a ledger of the
index masks is there and hands out an entry: not shown here. All four lemmas are stated at a Script
over the book: none is laid here. he at the number at which these lemmas take the name (the scalars
that the lookup's declared rounds count): `k4_he_at_head` (Law/W/HeAtHead.lean, of another writer)
has it under h; Law/W/LockAtHeadElems.lean spends it. Nor is it shown here that B is the book at
which these are had. The hypotheses: h; g below 12; hP: a hypothesis here (under the head at the
maker's return (`HeadAtReturn`) `k4PubG` returns at each g below 12: `k4_member_and_public_data`,
Law/ClosingLinePayers.lean); hB. That h can hold: the side library AtFullSide proves, with no
hypothesis, that h has a member at one place (AtFullSide.Top.headMember_zFull,
AtFullSide/Top/HeadMemberAtFull.lean, whose own Limits say what it is worth). No one term of Lean
joins that member, hP and a return of the maker. With the import of Law/W/LockAtHead.lean
come closed facts by evaluation in Lean's kernel (Law/W/MergeEndsAt.lean's six; those beneath
`k4IndexTakes_is`), which none of the rides beneath this file has put before an independent checker:
the five statements here call none of them. THE FULL SIZE ALONE, and the format's second hash function
alone. A program's walk from import to import, which reads import lines alone and stops unopened at
Johnson/Goal/, ThirdParty/, Johnson/D/, Johnson/Bridge/ and Cb/Bridge*, stopped at 74 modules under
Johnson/Goal/, at 7 under Johnson/Bridge/ and at 1 that begins Cb.Bridge: these counts are lower
bounds. A LAW, NOT A PART: no file that defines a part of the proof file's description may import
this one. Nothing on soundness, on completeness or on any other property. No property is claimed.

  `k4Lends_at_record`   at an opened description: the book lends K4's unseated row (a Bool)
  `k4Cut_at_record`   at an opened description: the book's cut at K4's place
  `k4Member_at_head`   a member of the head's own first chain at K4's place
  `k4Lends_at_head_of`   **lends, at the head's own description**
  `k4Cut_at_head_of`   **the cut, at the head's own description**
-/
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K4.Law.W.LockAtHead
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K4.Law.W.CutAtK4

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

/- no standing table of scales is in sight: a statement that reads a table says which -/
attribute [-instance] Inst.Model.Scl.ref

namespace ProofFile.Honest.K4.W
open OnBytes.Maker (WholeD)
open OnBytes.Desc.First.K4 (entries)
open OnBytes.Desc.First.K4.Honest
open VerifiableInference.Desc (Block Chain FileDescription)
open VerifiableInference.Desc.First (S)
open P5J (AtMgA TS)
open ProofFile.Honest.K4.Lot (k4PubG)

/-! ## 1 At the opened description -/

section
variable {P : VerifierAndGoals.PublicFiles} {pp : Inst.Model.ScalesAndPolicy} {lay : ByteArray} {F : FileDescription ProofFile.Inst}
  {Z : ProofFile.Pub} {Bs : ProofFile.PureBase} {base : List (Block S ProofFile.Cl)} {c : Chain S ProofFile.Cl}
  {A₂ : ProofFile.SharedSeat} {B₂ : ProofFile.SecondSeat} {gk : ℕ} {Q : K4Pub}
  {p0 p1 p2 : Johnson.G.ChainSends} {B : ProverCoinCounts}

/-- CONDITIONAL on hS, hR, O, hk, hQ, h and hp. **THE BOOK LENDS K4's ROW AS IT STANDS BEFORE IT IS
SEATED.** A Bool on public data. -/
theorem k4Lends_at_record (hS : VerifierAndGoals.InScope P = true) (hR : VerifierAndGoals.readFiles P = .ok pp)
    (O : IM.Open OnBytes.secondHashFunction P.pol lay P.KL F Z Bs base c A₂ B₂) (hk : gk < 12)
    (hQ : Q.P = Bs.G₀.W.layers ∧ Bs.G₀.W.G[gk]? = some Q.hp ∧ Q.g = gk ∧ Q.link = 2 * gk ∧
      Q.piece = 3)
    (h : bookWhole F p0 p1 p2 (mergesByName c.blocksInOrder) = .ok B) (hp : F.placesOk = true) :
    lendsRow B 0 (k4Place Q) (k4RowIn Q) = true := by
  obtain ⟨b, hb, hpl, hpl', hr⟩ := k4_member_there hS hR O hk hQ
  have hpos : K4Counts Q := k4Counts_at_group hS hR O hk hQ.1
  have hE : K4Ends Q := k4Ends_of_public O.public hQ.1
  have hl : b.place.link = some (2 * gk) := by rw [hpl']
  have eF := O.desc
  subst eF
  have hnd : (c.blocksInOrder.map (·.place)).Nodup := (ProofFile.Honest.places_nodup hp).1
  obtain ⟨A, m, R, -⟩ := k4_rowIsPlan_byName hnd hb hpl hr hpos hE
  exact k4_lends_whole h hp hb hl R (k4_noSeed hr)

/-- CONDITIONAL on hS, hR, O, hk, hQ, h and hp. **THE BOOK's CUT AT K4's PLACE IS THE NUMBERS OF
MOVES OF K4's SEATED ROW.** M is free: the cut does not read the list of merges. -/
theorem k4Cut_at_record (hS : VerifierAndGoals.InScope P = true) (hR : VerifierAndGoals.readFiles P = .ok pp)
    (O : IM.Open OnBytes.secondHashFunction P.pol lay P.KL F Z Bs base c A₂ B₂) (hk : gk < 12)
    (hQ : Q.P = Bs.G₀.W.layers ∧ Bs.G₀.W.G[gk]? = some Q.hp ∧ Q.g = gk ∧ Q.link = 2 * gk ∧
      Q.piece = 3)
    {M : Merges} (h : bookWhole F p0 p1 p2 M = .ok B) (hp : F.placesOk = true)
    {W₀ Rc Xi Tr X : Type} (cells : Tr → Cells) (weights : W₀ → Weights)
    (tokens : Xi → Array Nat) (look : List Fmt.Drawn → OnBytes.Model.Forest.Heard) :
    B.cuts.lookup (k4Place Q) =
      some ((k4Row (Rc := Rc) (X := X) Q cells weights tokens look).map (·.moves.length)) := by
  obtain ⟨b, hb, hpl, -, hr⟩ := k4_member_there hS hR O hk hQ
  have eF := O.desc
  subst eF
  rw [← hpl]
  exact k4_cut_fits h hp hb cells weights tokens look hpl hr

end

/-! ## 2 At the head -/

variable {Z : VerifierAndGoals.PublicFiles} {D : WholeD} {r : LPFD.Full.RunPF} {Zp : ProofFile.Pub} {Np : H2U.Places4}
  {cF : Chain TS ProofFile.Cl} {xh : VerifiableInference.Desc.First.Look.Place}

/-- The five equations on the lot's own public data, at the opening's public data. -/
private theorem five_at {Bs : ProofFile.PureBase} {g : ℕ} {Qp : K4Pub} (hW : Bs.G₀.W = Zp.p.X)
    (hP : k4PubG Zp g = some Qp) :
    Qp.P = Bs.G₀.W.layers ∧ Bs.G₀.W.G[g]? = some Qp.hp ∧ Qp.g = g ∧ Qp.link = 2 * g ∧
      Qp.piece = 3 := by
  obtain ⟨f1, f2, f3, f4, f5, _⟩ := k4PubG_fields hP
  exact ⟨by rw [hW]; exact f1, by rw [hW]; exact f2, f3, f4, f5⟩

/-- CONDITIONAL on h, hg and hP. **A MEMBER OF THE HEAD's OWN FIRST CHAIN AT K4's PLACE OF GROUP
g**, which declares K4's table's entries. No book stands in it. That it is the only one is not
drawn. -/
theorem k4Member_at_head (h : AtMgA OnBytes.secondHashFunction Z D r Zp Np cF xh) {g : ℕ} (hg : g < 12)
    {Qp : K4Pub} (hP : k4PubG Zp g = some Qp) :
    ∃ b ∈ cF.blocksInOrder, b.place = k4Place Qp ∧ b.place = IM.k4Place g ∧
      b.rounds = (entries Qp.P Qp.hp Qp.g).map fun e => ({ entry := e } : Fmt.DeclaredRound) := by
  obtain ⟨Bs, base, O⟩ := h.laid.opened
  exact k4_member_there h.scope h.reads O hg (five_at O.W hP)

/-- CONDITIONAL on h, hg, hP and hB. **THE BOOK LENDS K4's ROW AS IT STANDS BEFORE IT IS SEATED, AT
THE HEAD's OWN DESCRIPTION.** A Bool on public data. The three lists of sendings are free letters.
-/
theorem k4Lends_at_head_of (h : AtMgA OnBytes.secondHashFunction Z D r Zp Np cF xh) {g : ℕ} (hg : g < 12)
    {Qp : K4Pub} (hP : k4PubG Zp g = some Qp) {B : ProverCoinCounts}
    {p0 p1 p2 : Johnson.G.ChainSends}
    (hB : bookWhole (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) p0 p1 p2 (mergesByName cF.blocksInOrder) = .ok B) :
    lendsRow B 0 (k4Place Qp) (k4RowIn Qp) = true := by
  obtain ⟨Bs, base, O⟩ := h.laid.opened
  exact k4Lends_at_record h.scope h.reads O hg (five_at O.W hP) hB
    (Johnson.RunOne.Sound.placesOk_of_planOk _ h.laid.planOk)

/-- CONDITIONAL on h, hg, hP and hB. **THE BOOK's CUT AT K4's PLACE, AT THE HEAD's OWN
DESCRIPTION.** The three lists of sendings are free letters. -/
theorem k4Cut_at_head_of (h : AtMgA OnBytes.secondHashFunction Z D r Zp Np cF xh) {g : ℕ} (hg : g < 12)
    {Qp : K4Pub} (hP : k4PubG Zp g = some Qp) {B : ProverCoinCounts}
    {p0 p1 p2 : Johnson.G.ChainSends}
    (hB : bookWhole (P5J.F0T OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp Np cF) p0 p1 p2 (mergesByName cF.blocksInOrder) = .ok B)
    {W₀ Rc Xi Tr X : Type} (cells : Tr → Cells) (weights : W₀ → Weights)
    (tokens : Xi → Array Nat) (look : List Fmt.Drawn → OnBytes.Model.Forest.Heard) :
    B.cuts.lookup (k4Place Qp) =
      some ((k4Row (Rc := Rc) (X := X) Qp cells weights tokens look).map (·.moves.length)) := by
  obtain ⟨Bs, base, O⟩ := h.laid.opened
  exact k4Cut_at_record h.scope h.reads O hg (five_at O.W hP) hB
    (Johnson.RunOne.Sound.placesOk_of_planOk _ h.laid.planOk) cells weights tokens look

end ProofFile.Honest.K4.W

#print axioms ProofFile.Honest.K4.W.k4Lends_at_record
#print axioms ProofFile.Honest.K4.W.k4Cut_at_record
#print axioms ProofFile.Honest.K4.W.k4Member_at_head
#print axioms ProofFile.Honest.K4.W.k4Lends_at_head_of
#print axioms ProofFile.Honest.K4.W.k4Cut_at_head_of
